<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.2.3 Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00718</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.2.3 Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8ae7a9c2-4bba-497f-b8fc-1ba52c3fe84a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>The table below shows the revenue for the number of pizzas sold at a restaurant.</para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Number of Pizzas</entry>
      <entry>20</entry>
      <entry>30</entry>
      <entry>40</entry>
      <entry>50</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Revenue</entry>
      <entry>110</entry>
      <entry>160</entry>
      <entry>210</entry>
      <entry>260</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<para>Which linear model could be used to predict the revenue if 4000 pizzas were sold?</para></section>
</content>
</document>
